  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Southeast Asian Ministers of Education Organisation: Membership</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Funding under this investment represents Australia&apos;s annual associate membership core contribution, coordinated by the Australian Department of Education, to the Southeast Asian Ministers of Education Organisation (SEAMEO). SEAMEO is a regional intergovernmental organization established in 1965 among governments of Southeast Asian countries to promote regional cooperation in education, science and culture in South East Asia. SEAMEO&apos;s mission is to enhance regional understanding, cooperation and unity of purpose among Member Countries for a better quality of life through the establishment of networks and partnerships, the provision of fora among policy makers and experts, and the promotion of sustainable human resource development.</narrative>
  </description>
